<rml>
<head>
    <link type="text/rcss" href="theme.rcss"/>
    <link type="text/rcss" href="examineitem.rcss"/>
</head>
<body data-model="examineitem">
    <!-- Tier 3 entry (examine_item_menu). First consumer of the F.2 item-info
         component (rml_util::item_info_rml_lines). Title (item name) + a left
         action list (the existing add_entry actions: hotkey + name, hint colour,
         cursor) + the right item-info pane (#examine-info) rendering the shared
         item-info lines. The legacy is a contextual SIDE PANEL beside the parent
         inventory; this is a FULL-SCREEN doc that covers the parent instead
         (conscious simplification — the item is already chosen). It is the FIRST
         RmlUi modal opened NESTED over a still-active curses parent. Actions stay
         on input_context: keyboard UP/DOWN select + CONFIRM/hotkey run; mouse
         SELECTS an action (run via Enter — click-to-run not supported, per the
         mouse-selects/keyboard-acts invariant). PAGE_UP/DOWN scroll #examine-info. -->
    <div class="panel ei-panel">
        <div class="ei-title" data-rml="title_rml"></div>
        <div class="ei-main">
            <div class="ei-actions scroll-pane">
                <div class="ei-action" data-for="a : actions"
                     data-class-selected="a.selected"
                     data-event-mouseover="on_action(it_index)"
                     data-event-click="on_action(it_index)"
                     data-rml="a.name_rml"></div>
            </div>
            <div id="examine-info" class="ei-info scroll-pane">
                <div class="ei-line" data-for="ln : info" data-rml="ln.text_rml"></div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</body>
</rml>
